"Publicity Clause: The Parties agree that each Party shall have the right to use the other Party's logo in connection with its own promotional materials, subject to the following conditions:
(i) The Party seeking to use the other Party's logo shall provide the other Party with thirty (30) days' written notice of its intention to use the logo;
(ii) The Party seeking to use the other Party's logo shall provide the other Party with a sample of the intended use of the logo;
(iii) The other Party shall have the right to approve or disapprove the intended use of the logo within ten (10) days of receiving the notice and sample;
(iv) If the other Party disapproves the intended use of the logo, the Party seeking to use the logo shall not use it;
(v) The Party seeking to use the other Party's logo shall include a disclaimer on its promotional materials stating that the other Party does not endorse or sponsor the Party's products or services.

